// Paper summaries. Hand-maintained, and NOT touched by the daily Sheet sync (which rebuilds
// only RESEARCH_DATA). Rules, shape and how to add one: docs/paper-summaries.md.
//
// Keyed by RESEARCH_DATA id. A paper listed here shows its summary in the Papers tab in place of its
// key finding and bullets; every other paper is unchanged. The first twelve entries were the pilot; on
// 2026-11-11 the rollout to the other papers began (see "Rollout" in docs/paper-summaries.md). Every
// entry is an unreviewed draft written from saved source text. Only papers that are not archived in the
// Sheet get an entry: the console validator flags an entry whose paper is not in RESEARCH_DATA.
//   lede      one sentence: the central claim or finding (35 words at most)
//   body      what the authors did and found (75 words at most)
//   note      optional: how much weight the evidence can bear (60 words at most). Shown as "Take note".
//   basis     "full text" or "abstract only" (an abstract-only summary has no note)
//   basisNote optional: what exactly was read, shown in brackets after the basis ("the arXiv version")
//   written   date the summary was written
//   reviewed  date a person checked it against the source, or null while it is a draft
//   model     what wrote it
// No result figures (percentages, dollar amounts, effect sizes) in the prose: those live in the Fact
// Bank, where they are quoted and rated. No em-dashes.
